Assert.IsTrue(_email.WasNotificationSent(order.Id));
```

**Risk:** Non-deterministic — 2 s may be too short on a loaded CI agent, or wastefully long otherwise. Slows the entire suite.

**Fix — use a polling helper or make the fake synchronous:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    processor.ProcessOrderAsync(order);

    // Wait for the signal the fake sets when notification is sent
    Assert.IsTrue(
        await _email.WaitForNotificationAsync(order.Id, timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5)));
}
```

