### MEDIUM Severity

#### 5. Eager Test
**Ref:** testsmells.org — *Eager Test*  
**Location:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (lines 57–63)

```csharp
// ❌ 7 distinct production methods called in one test
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);

Assert.AreEqual("Completed", order.Status);
```

**Risk:** When this test fails, any of 7 methods could be the cause. Diagnosis requires stepping through all of them.

**Fix — break into focused tests per behavior, or mark explicitly as an integration test:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Integration")]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { /* ... keep as-is ... */ }
```
Or better — test each method individually and keep only a clearly-labelled workflow smoke test.

